Blocker: any path beyond the 19, or a byte under `api/`, `.github`, `infra`, `scripts/`, `web/src/server`, `web/package.json`/lock, `playwright.config.ts`, or in `followUpFailure`/a partner follow-up screen (STOP, tier 1); a shipped string that differs from the ruled pack by one byte; an old string still on a screen (`coming later`, the old 8a body, `Partner Dashboard` as an h1, the old 7a body on the client page); an unchanged string changed (K1-K7); a rendered string different from the source string; a skip/removal/weakened assertion; the 12 red rows not red at base for their stated cause, or a new row green at base; a mutant of W1-W3, D1-D3, H1, P1, C1-C2, K8 that no row turns red; any red at head in the unit suite, typecheck, lint, build or `--check-shards` that base passes; a lost test name beyond the one rename; one of the five edited e2e specs red at head; a string overflowing sideways at 320 px; a time string taken from the SERVER's zone or a hydration mismatch on a screen that shows a time; a Jira comment that is false (the "-ise" premise repeated) or carries a name/secret; a secret; a request that left loopback; a merge conflict with current main; overlap with any live branch > 0. Major: any of W4, C3, C4 that no row turns red (survivor); a builder claim your measurement contradicts (19 paths, 6 commits, 12 red of 100, lost 1 / added 14, 2056 / 2069 / 186 files, 9 build warnings equal to main's, the Chrome placeholder sizes, the four zone strings); the instrument control not firing; a process or port of yours left behind; the load discipline broken without figures; a pack-vs-brief difference in a string (even if the code follows the pack). Minor: a taste item on a wrapped label at 320 px; the source-text rows that pin wording the screen test also pins; a comment in the diff that names a card rather than a ticket. **Notes (NOT failures):** no CI on a PR-less branch; the B461 sequenced line `:155` until the one-line follow-up lands (a sequencing fact, with the exact diff in FOR TUESDAY); the non-Australian reader's `GMT-7` (facts for Tuesday's card, ruled by nobody here); the possibly unreachable notice button (same); `SendFollowUp.tsx:88` shows a date, not a time; CodeQL not run; the one flaky neighbour unless reproduced as stated. Overall **GO** · **GO WITH FINDINGS** · **NO GO**; HPSMPOC-148 and HPSMPOC-310 get a verdict each. First line of STATUS: `GATE VERDICT B474: <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> @ c65a5ab (delta <19 paths, 6 commits, bytes outside the 19 = 0 y/n, skips 0 y/n> · words <n of 14 strings equal to the pack, old strings left n, rendered equal n of 5> · prior work <history matches y/n, Done-when met y/n per ticket, Jira comments true y/n> · red-first <red at base n of 12, never-red rows n> · mutants <W1-W4 D1-D3 H1 P1 C1-C4 K8 killed n of 14, survivors <names|none>> · suites <vitest n files n/n head vs n/n base vs n/n merged, names lost n added n, typecheck/lint/build/shards ok y/n, 5 repeats n/5, signin-budget note> · browser <five specs desktop n/n mobile n/n, base-red y/n, 320 px overflow n, requests off loopback n> · sequencing <merge clean y/n, spec :155 red y/n, one-line follow-up named y/n> · facts <zones measured n of 11 in node and chrome, server-vs-reader zone <reader|server|n/a>, notice button <reachable|unreachable>> · merge <clean|conflict>, overlap telemetry n, b459 n, b460 n, b461 n, b462 n, b467 n, b466 <n|branch absent> · CI <none|state> · gitleaks rc <n>)`. Then Step 0 sha256s and slot count · REFUSE counts · PINS (start, mid, verdict: branch name beside each sha; b461 and the other seats' branches read only to show them unmoved by you) · instrument (node, Playwright version, browser build, load per heavy start, time waited) · checks 1-8 each with FAIL (clock), evidence path, result · findings `B474-n` (severity, `path:line` at the head, instrument, FAIL met, fix-shape in prose, evidence class MEASURED AT RUNTIME / PROBED / READ ONLY) · FOR TUESDAY (no PR yet: Tuesday opens it on GO/GWF a